# Catalog runtime bridge

Generated by `ng generate @infra-tools/agentic-ui:connect-studio`. This folder
connects the app to an **Experience Studio** catalog backend: it loads the
tenant's governed capabilities at boot and keeps them live over SSE, so a change
authored in Studio appears here without a rebuild or reload.

## What it wires

| Catalog kind | Compiled into | Rendered/used by |
|---|---|---|
| `experience` | `ExperienceRegistry` | the planner / experience host |
| `form`       | `FormRegistry`       | `<mvk-form-renderer [formName]>` |
| `workflow`   | `FormRegistry` (`.workflow`) | `<mvk-workflow-renderer [formName]>` |
| `datasource` | `DataSourceRegistry` | tools, at call time |
| `tool`       | `ToolRegistry`       | the assistant |

Each source registers rows tagged with a `source`, so a re-hydrate cleanly
`removeBySource(...)` and replaces the previous set.

## Configuration

Wired in `app.config.ts`:

```ts
provideCatalogRuntime({
  baseUrl: 'http://localhost:8081',   // catalog service
  tenant: 'acme',                     // your catalog id
  // authMode: 'oidc',                // default 'disabled'
  // dataSourceSecrets: { CRM_TOKEN: '…' },  // ${CRM_TOKEN} in data-source headers
})
```

`provideCatalogRuntime` must sit **alongside** `provideAgenticUi()` /
`provideAgenticUiPlatform()` — the lib platform provides the registries this
bridge fills. If you haven't installed it, run `ng add @infra-tools/agentic-ui`
first.

## OIDC

In `authMode: 'oidc'` the client forwards a bearer token from `CATALOG_AUTH`.
Point it at your existing auth service (must expose `token(): string | null`):

```ts
{ provide: CATALOG_AUTH, useExisting: MyAuthService }
```

## Connection status

Every source exposes `count` and `error` signals — inject one to show a live
indicator:

```ts
private readonly forms = inject(CatalogFormSource);
protected readonly formCount = this.forms.count;   // e.g. 11
```

## Extending

The bridge covers the registry-backed content kinds. To also load
`kind:'navigation' | 'prompt' | 'skill' | 'theme' | 'decision' | 'validation'`,
add a source next to these following the same shape (`listByKind` → compile via
the matching `agenticX(...)` factory → `register` tagged with a source →
`onMutation` re-hydrate) and call it from `provideCatalogRuntime`.
